description: Enforce one-line human-readable git commit messages
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commit Message Format

- Use one sentence only, imperative mood, human-readable.
- Keep the subject line under 72 characters.
- Use a type prefix: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`, or `chore:`.
- Do not include a multi-line body unless the user explicitly asks for one.
- Never include AI attribution (`Co-authored-by`, `Generated-by`, etc.).
